{"title":"2005 CEMC Hypatia Problems/Problem 2b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 CEMC Hypatia Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Gwen and Chris are playing a game. They begin with a pile of toothpicks, and use the following rules:\n</p>\n<ul style=\"li-style-type: disc\">\n<li>The two players alternate turns</li>\n<li>On any turn, the player can remove 1, 2, 3, 4, or 5 toothpicks from the pile</li>\n<li>The same number of toothpicks cannot be removed on two different turns</li>\n<li>The last person who is able to play wins, regardless of whether there are any toothpicks remaining in the pile</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For example, if the game begins with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> toothpicks, the following moves could occur:\n</p>\n<dl><dd>Gwen removes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> toothpick, leaving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the pile</dd>\n<dd>Chris removes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> toothpicks, leaving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the pile</dd>\n<dd>Gwen removes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> toothpicks, leaving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the pile</dd></dl>\n<p>Gwen is now the winner, since Chris cannot remove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> toothpick. (Gwen already removed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> toothpick on one of her turns, and the third rule says that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> toothpick cannot be removed on another turn.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose the game begins with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> toothpicks. Gwen begins by removing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> toothpicks. Explain why Gwen can always win, regardless of what Chris removes on his turn.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, after Gwen removes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> toothpicks, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/3/283f867a2fabbe1739b1ee12fc4611f5e93aa9ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 - 5 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> toothpicks remaining. However, Chris must remove from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> toothpicks based on rules 1 and rules 3 because only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> toothpicks can be removed and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> toothpicks were already removed in a previous turn.\n</p><p>Gwen wins no matter what Chris chooses as a result, as the integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can be paired to sum up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> toothpicks remaining. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/4530292c1b1efae89118ebf5a50da1a905739e47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 4 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/27803b32e1de1532968c2bc198dd16b640f3e4b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 3 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, meaning:\n</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If Chris removes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> toothpick, Gwen could just remove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> toothpicks and vice versa.\n</li><li>If Chris removes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> toothpicks, Gwen could just remove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> toothpicks and vice versa.\n</li></ul>\n<p>Thus, Gwen can always win, no matter what Chris chooses.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017205503\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.032 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 102/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1296/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4985/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.864      1 2005_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%    8.864      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35656:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017205503 and revision id 278125. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}